<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zaporozhian Cossacks</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16th–18th centuries</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Zaporozhians</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Zaporozhian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossacks</a> were the Cossacks of the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dnieper">Dnieper</a>, organised from the 16th century around the fortified Zaporozhian Sich beyond the river's rapids. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohdan-khmelnytsky">Bohdan Khmelnytsky</a> they led the rising of 1648 against Poland-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> that created the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossack-hetmanate">Cossack Hetmanate</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catherine-the-great">Catherine the Great</a> destroyed the Sich in 1775, and many former Zaporozhians were later resettled as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> Cossack Host in the Kuban.</p></div>
